# PART 3 — The film

**Title:** Marque — Agents you can hold to account
**Runtime:** 2:40 (±5s, hard ceiling 2:50) · 1920×1080 · 30fps (60 if the render budget allows)
**Structure:** one question, asked at 0:04, answered at 2:32.

### 3.1 The spine

The strongest asset in this product is a number nobody else can show:

> **163 conformance runs against third-party agents on BNB Smart Chain. Zero passes.**

That is the film. Not "here are our features." The question is *how many of these three hundred thousand agents can actually do the job*, and the answer is a measured, uncomfortable, verifiable number. Everything else in the product exists to make that answer trustworthy.

This also solves the framing problem in Part 0.2: the film never says "four warranted." It says something far stronger and entirely honest.

### 3.2 Full script

Every number below is a **draft to be verified against the live product at capture time.** If a figure has moved, the bot rewrites the line and re-synthesises that sentence. Never ship a number the product does not currently show.

