# PART 5 — Acceptance gates

The film is not finished until every one of these is true.

| Gate | Requirement |
|---|---|
| Truth | Every number spoken and shown matches FACTS.json, read live from the product. No figure is estimated, rounded in our favour, or carried over from a draft. |
| Labels | Every shot carries its corner label. Mainnet, testnet, archive and explanatory graphic are never confused. No graphic impersonates a product surface. |
| Voice | A human listened to three candidates and chose. If we shipped local TTS, the deliverable says so plainly. |
| Narration-led | No speech time-stretched above 1.03×. Runtime was achieved by cutting copy, not by speeding the voice. |
| Resolution | No shot is upscaled. Every push is a crop of a larger source. Text is legible at 100% on every push frame. |
| Captions | Word-level forced alignment, verified in playback, nothing masking evidence, no duplicate subtitle track. |
| Silence | The 1.5 seconds at "Passes: zero" are genuinely silent. |
| Mix | Encoded final measures −14 ±1 LUFS, TP ≤ −1.0. Someone listened on a laptop and a phone. |
| Muted | The first eight seconds are comprehensible with the sound off. |
| Runtime | ≤ 2:50. |
| Honesty | No claim of an Altana integration. No claim of a listening or review step that was not performed. |

